MODIFICATIONS
-------------

Modified by Symp's, from 2025 onwards. Carried changes, relative to the
original Upscayl codebase:

- Rebranding to "Symp's Upscale"
- Migration from Electron to a Tauri 2.x backend
- Redesigned user interface, in French
- Print sizing in centimetres with an output-resolution target
- Chained x4 inference passes to reach an exact target width
- Output resolution (DPI) written into the saved file
- EXIF orientation baked in before upscaling
- Workload guard rails for large-format jobs
- Automatic cutting of the finished image into numbered hanging strips
- Built-in user guide covering every setting
- Added the 4xLSDIRCompactC3 model (CC BY 4.0, attributed below) as the
  default, measured both more faithful and far faster than the inherited
  models, and retired both inherited models, which it outperformed
- Progress, cancel and various UX fixes

The AI models themselves are NOT modified: they are shipped byte-for-byte as
received (see the checksums below).


