B. Models inherited from Upscayl — none remain

Both models inherited from the Upscayl distribution (`upscayl-standard-4x`
and `upscayl-lite-4x`) were retired in version 1.5. Measured over 32 images
by a 4x round-trip, neither was the most faithful often enough to justify
keeping it: the standard model was never best on any image and ran about 26x
slower than the default, and the lite model was slower than the default on
every one of the 32 while scoring lower overall. Together they accounted for
roughly 33 MB of the download.

This also removes the only models whose licence could not be established:
Upscayl ships no licence file for its model weights. Every model bundled
today has a licence documented at its author's own source.

A model a user loads through the custom-models feature is not distributed
with this software and carries whatever terms its own author set — several
widely circulated upscaling models are published under CC BY-NC terms, which
do not permit commercial use.


